<title>POLAND: ZLOTY FIXED STRONGER AT 3.25 PCT FROM PARITY RATE.</title>
<headline>ZLOTY FIXED STRONGER AT 3.25 PCT FROM PARITY RATE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.1195 to the dollar, up from 3.1300 on Tuesday and at 1.8080 to the mark, down from 1.8060, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.25 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Tuesday's 3.11 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
